<v SPEAKER_12>What the fuck happened to music, guys? What happened to the music? Let me just say this shit real quick. And if it pisses you off, maybe you're the one I'm talking to. And I promise, this comes from the most loving place possible here. I've met musicians who spend 20 hours a day crafting the perfect solo for a 30 second Instagram clip multi-tracked, color graded, edited to death, that splice together nine takes just to play something they could never reproduce live. And yet, ask them to play over a simple blues progression in front of a real human being. And it's like watching a deer get hit by a truck. Like what the fuck happened to the music? What happened to sitting with your instrument and spending time learning music, transcribing, training your ears, composing, reading books? What happened to all of that? Now we just chase numbers, chase likes, chase fake ass approval. Since when did Instagram become our manager, a teacher and our audience somehow? We've confused visibility with value. We've confused content with craft. We've confused attention with art.

